SCIM now echoes the canonical email `type` of `"work"` on stored user emails, so
that PATCH value-path filters like Entra's `emails[type eq "work"].value` match
the existing entry for an in-place update. Previously spar synthesized emails
with no `type`; the value-path filter then matched no entry, and since per
RFC 7644 §3.5.2 an `Add` on a non-existing target creates it (rather than
erroring), every such PATCH appended a duplicate email instead of updating the
address in place.
